    "created_at": "2021-05-13T14:53:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-05-13T14:53:04Z",
    "body": "> Whereas your proposed rotateAxis() is equivalent to CSS's rotate3d(). I'd argue in favor of naming consistency, and I'm also concerned about the 3-angle form being confusing.\r\n\r\nThe thinking here was that it would be more valuable to match popular and well established 3d APIs like three.js, unreal and Unity as opposed to CSS in this instance. `rotateAxis` is definitely more useful than the `rotate3d` Euler rotations, but the most requested use cases are things like card flipping and text crawls. In lieu of adding three separate `rotateX`, `rotateY`, `rotateZ` functions, we decided to go with just one. Euler angles always get surprising when pushed to their limits, this feels like a limitation of most 3d platforms.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
