    "updated_at": "2024-11-26T17:12:43Z",
    "body": "From my understanding the hesitation was because of Webkit using Cairo in 2021 but now in 2024 based on this https://blogs.igalia.com/carlosgc/2024/09/27/graphics-improvements-in-webkitgtk-and-wpewebkit-2-46/ shouldn't this be looked at again? It seems the first thing that needs to be settled on is the API interface. I like the rotateX, rotateY, rotateZ idea personally. If we can land on this a polyfill can be worked on and hopefully this can be moved forward on?",
